Time: 15 seconds

Slide 2: Executive Summary

Speak:

Insurance customer information is usually fragmented across policies, claims, payments and customer interactions.

Agents spend time searching for information and manually connecting the customer story before choosing an action.

Insure360 AI brings this context into one Streamlit workspace. It uses Snowflake Cortex AI to generate customer insights and grounded answers, while deterministic business rules recommend the next best action.

The outcome is simple: understand the customer faster, explain what matters and take the next best action.

The deck defines the solution as one workspace combining Customer 360, timeline, analytics, AI insights and an action workflow.

Time: 30 seconds

Slide 3: Problem Brief

Speak:

The current customer-service journey has four main problems.

First, agents must search across multiple operational systems.

Second, they manually assemble policy, payment, claim and interaction context.

Third, unstructured call transcripts are difficult to consume during a live customer interaction.

Finally, the next action can depend on individual interpretation rather than a consistent workflow.

The opportunity is to make customer context immediately usable through unified history, explainable AI-assisted insight and a repeatable action process.

These four stages and the opportunity statement are presented on the Problem Brief slide.

Time: 30 seconds

Slide 4: Solution Overview

Point to each section while speaking.

Speak:

The solution follows a simple four-stage journey.

Monitor: understand portfolio-level risk, claims, payments and renewals.

Understand: open a Customer 360 profile and review the complete customer timeline.

Assist: use AI-generated executive briefs, interaction summaries and grounded natural-language questions.

Act: review the explainable Next Best Action, approve or reject it and retain the decision in the audit trail.

It is one workspace, one customer story and one informed next step.

The four-stage Monitor, Understand, Assist and Act flow is the central solution structure in the deck.

Time: 30 seconds

Slide 5: Architecture

Speak:

At the foundation, the solution uses five data domains: customers, policies, claims, payments and customer call transcripts.

The structured records and unstructured interactions are unified through Snowflake views into the Customer 360 and customer journey layers.

The analytics layer provides portfolio KPIs, distributions and operational signals.

The decision layer contains eight deterministic Next Best Action rules. Every recommendation includes its rule ID, priority, confidence, reasoning and estimated business impact.

Cortex AI generates interaction digests and executive briefs. A semantic view and Cortex Agent support the grounded AI architecture.

Everything is surfaced through a Streamlit application with approval and audit capabilities.

The architecture is presented as a Snowflake-native flow from structured and unstructured data to governed action.

Time: 40 seconds

Slide 6: CoCo CLI Lifecycle

Speak:

CoCo CLI, through Cortex Code, was used across the full implementation lifecycle.

During planning, it helped design the architecture, data model, gap analysis and roadmap.

During development, it generated SQL views, synthetic data, semantic-model artifacts, agent definitions and Streamlit code.

During validation, it tested referential integrity, KPI realism, the eight recommendation rules and anti-hallucination behavior.

During execution, it uploaded and deployed the Streamlit application and helped resolve runtime compatibility issues.

This resulted in nine generated implementation artifacts, fourteen successful backend validations, eight deterministic rules and a deployed Streamlit application.

The CoCo lifecycle slide covers planning, building, validation and deployment, including nine artifacts, 14 validations and eight rules.

